Task: Pegar refresca la copia viva y lo armado (Fase 7, pattern-copy_20260910)

Green phase. `PatternPasteRefresh` decides, and `pastePattern()` acts on it:

- Destination equal to the loaded slot → `pattern` and `ControlInput` adopt what
  was pasted. Without this the track screen kept showing the previous material
  and `recordEdit()` wrote it back over the paste on the first knob turn — the
  paste was lost with no warning.
- Destination equal to the armed slot → the same slot is armed again with the new
  material, and the pending adoption stores the new one. Without this the
  transport still held the snapshot handed to it at arming time, so the old
  material entered at the bar boundary. That was the reported symptom: what was
  pasted did not sound until the Pattern was triggered by hand again.

Neither arms a different slot nor moves the selection, which is what FR10
forbids. Audio still does not cut (FR9): nothing is published to the transport
outside the re-arm, so what sounds keeps sounding until the next Pattern change.

